<TITLE>O2 Sensor</TITLE>
<LIST1 TYPE = "UNORDERED"><ITEM><PTXT>Converts the oxygen concentration in the exhaust gas into an electromotive force and detects whether the air-fuel ratio is rich or lean relative to the stoichiometric air-fuel ratio.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>By heating the sensor (zirconia element) with a built-in heater, the O<SUB>2</SUB>sensor temperature is kept constant, promoting feedback control.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1>
